Interpretation: raw byte inequality alone is not sufficient; a FIXED generation may keep the same 64 KiB Normal starter and merely re-index it. Exact scalar-multiset equality and full q256 replay therefore count as underlying sample-pool reuse, even when the emitted chunk byte sequence differs.
